items.statement:
Let \(E\) be a subset of a metric space \(X\). Then \(E^\circ\) is the
largest open subset of \(X\) contained in \(E\). In other words:
- \(E^\circ\subseteq E\);
- \(E^\circ\) is open;
- \(E^\circ\supseteq O\), for every open set \(O\subseteq E\).

